<article class="env-lemma" id="0GIZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GIZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0GIZ">59.66.3</span>.</a> Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. Let $\ell $ be a prime number and $n \geq 1$. Let $H$ be a finite $\ell $-group. Let $M$ be a finite $\Lambda [H]$-module annihilated by $\ell ^ n$. Then there is a finite filtration $0 = M_0 \subset M_1 \subset \ldots \subset M_ t = M$ by $\Lambda [H]$-submodules such that $H$ acts trivially on $M_{i + 1}/M_ i$ for all $i = 0, \ldots , t - 1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: Show that the augmentation ideal $\mathfrak m$ of the noncommutative ring $\mathbf{Z}/\ell ^ n\mathbf{Z}[H]$ is nilpotent. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>